# Monica Rambeau (3/3 flying, prowess; "{2}{R}{W}{W}: Transform Monica Rambeau. Activate only as a sorcery."), back face Photon, Living
# Light (4/4 flying, hexproof, prowess; "Whenever you cast a noncreature spell, put a +1/+1 counter on each other creature you control").
# Turn 1: Monica is cast, then a Mox (a noncreature spell) gives her prowess: a 4/4 until the end of turn. Turn 3: she transforms for
# {2}{R}{W}{W} (only as a sorcery: refused on turn 2, Bot2's turn) and becomes Photon, the same permanent; casting another Mox then gives Photon its own prowess (5/5 for the turn) and
# puts one counter on Bot1's other creature, the Ornithopter, but not on Photon herself or on Bot2's Ornithopter. Bot2's Lightning
# Bolt can't target Photon (hexproof).

